sequenceDiagram
    title GATT Read/Write Example: Reading PLX Features and Enabling Notifications

    participant Product as Product<br>[implements GattClientResponse]
    participant CN as CN<br>[implements GattClient]

    note over Product, CN: Precondition: connected, GATT discovery complete.<br>PLX service handles 64..69 are known.

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: Read PLX Features characteristic
        Product->>CN: ReadCharacteristic(69)
        CN-->>Product: ReadCharacteristicResponse(<br>data={handle=69, data=0x0700})
        CN-->>Product: OperationComplete(success)

        note over Product: 0x0700 = supported features bitmask.<br>Bits indicate: SpO2, pulse rate, measurement status.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: Enable notifications on PLX Continuous Measurement
        Product->>CN: WriteDescriptor(handle=67, data=0x0100)
        CN-->>Product: OperationComplete(success)

        note over Product: Wrote 0x0100 to CCCD (handle 67).<br>Notifications are now enabled for value handle 66.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: Write without response (fire-and-forget)
        Product->>CN: WriteCharacteristicWithoutResponse(<br>handle=69, data=0x01)

        note over Product: No OperationComplete for WriteWithoutResponse.<br>Next operation can be issued immediately.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: Sequential operations
        Product->>CN: ReadDescriptor(67)
        CN-->>Product: ReadDescriptorResponse(<br>data={handle=67, data=0x0100})
        CN-->>Product: OperationComplete(success)

        note over Product: CCCD reads back 0x0100, confirming notifications are enabled.
    end
